  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Waves**: rare: 8 archived performances [3]\n- **Pungee**: back after 21 archived shows (1583 days); rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Africa**: back after 21 archived shows (1583 days); rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Iko Iko**: back after 39 archived shows (1952 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Look-Ka Py Py**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Keep On Marching**: back after 21 archived shows (1583 days); rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **I Need More Time**: back after 20 archived shows (1582 days); rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **He Bite Me (The Dragon)**: back after 21 archived shows (1583 days); rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2019-07-19.cmc621.cmc641vxt.sbd.matrix.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 17 songs; 143 min [1]. Said about its sound: This is the 24-bit version of the matrix recording, not meant for CD burning; a 16-bit version exists separately [1]\n- **soulive2019-07-19.cmc621.cmc641vxt.sbd.matrix.flac16**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 17 songs; 143 min [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2019-07-19.cmc621.cmc641vxt.sbd.matrix.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Mics/Room Mics/SBD Matrix [1]. Also: Two Schoeps mics (one on stage, one at the front-of-house booth) plus a soundboard feed, all recorded through a Sonosax preamp to a Sound Devices 788T at 24/96 [1]\n- **soulive2019-07-19.cmc621.cmc641vxt.sbd.matrix.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Mics/Room Mics/SBD Matrix [2]. Also: Two Schoeps mics (stage and front-of-house) plus an Avid Profile soundboard feed were recorded via Sonosax into a Sound Devices 788T at 24/96; Eric McRoberts recorded, edited and mixed it on July 20-21, 2019, using SoundForge and Vegas Pro, with downsampling and dithering to 16-bit/44.1 [2]",
